ation, gaming, or typical inference.\n- **Mode 2:** Better multi-tenant or multi-context scenarios where you want more balanced CCS distribution.\n- **Mode 4:** High-performance compute where you want to fully utilize all compute slices with dedicated CCS\u2014useful for server/cluster workloads, heavy parallel compute, or when you observe CCS contention bottlenecks.\n\n---\n\n**Important caveat:** I want to be upfront that the exact numeric semantics of these `ccs_mode` values aren't something I can state with full confidence from memory, and they can shift between driver versions. The `xe` driver is under very active development, and these parameters have evolved.\n\nI'd strongly recommend verifying against"}